-- title:
--   Existence of place-level reductions red₁,red₂ for X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $p$, a nonzero natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Further, $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise images under `coeffEmb L` of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Next, $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as its fraction field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and $K$ carries an $A$-algebra structure making $A \to L \to K$ a scalar tower. Finally $j \in K$ has Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), and $j \neq 0$. Throughout, $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ denotes the two-chart $A$-model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), assumed proper, whose finite chart is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) of $K$.
--
--   **Residue data and special-fibre components.** An algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra; schemes $C_1, C_2$ with structure morphisms $c_1, c_2$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, each proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral; morphisms $i_1, i_2$ from $C_1, C_2$ to the base change $X_k =$ `baseChange A (modelTo A K j) k` over the respective structure maps, both closed immersions. The hypothesis `hcover` says every point of the pullback $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred` says the scheme-theoretic intersection `pullback i₁.1 i₂.1` is reduced, and `hn`, `hn0` say its cardinality is $n$ with $0 < n$.
--
--   **Sections.** A section $\varepsilon$ of $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, sections $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ of $c_1, c_2$, and `hε₁`: $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base-changed section `sectionBaseChange k ε`.
--
--   **Relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ data (summarised here).** A designation $D$ over $A$ for $X$ (a scheme $D.P$ with structure map $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section), together with: `hrep`, the nonempty assertion that $D$ represents the sub-Picard functor cut out by `algEquivZeroCut` (fibrewise algebraically-trivial rigidified line bundles) for $(X, \varepsilon)$; `hsm` and `hsep`, smoothness and separatedness of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$; `hreps`, the corresponding representability over $k$ for $(X_k, \varepsilon_k)$ by $D_k = D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k$; `hPk`, an isomorphism of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` with the base change to $k$ of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along `pullback.fst D.toBase (specMap A k)`; designations $D_1, D_2$ over $k$ for $c_1, c_2$ with representability data `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`; and a morphism $\nu_2$ from $D_k.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ together with `hν₂`, which states that for every $k$-scheme $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and every $T$-point $a$ of $D_k.\mathrm{toBase}$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification along `rigSection c₂ t ε₂` of the pullback along `curveChange i₂.1 i₂.2 t` of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` along $a$; thus $\nu_2$ is the restriction map on relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ induced by $i_2$.
--
--   **Geometric generic fibre.** A curve model $M_\eta$ over $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$ of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), i.e. a proper smooth integral curve with an identification of its function field and a bijection between its closed points and the places; an isomorphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ to $X_{\bar{\mathbb{Q}}} =$ `pullback (modelTo A K j) (specMap A (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` with `heη` saying $e_\eta$ followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec}\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$; a nonemptiness hypothesis on the open subscheme of $M_\eta.C$ obtained as the preimage, under $e_\eta$ followed by `pullback.fst`, of the image of the finite chart; `hMηpin`, which says that for each $a$ in the finite chart algebra, the element of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` obtained by pulling $a$ back to that open and taking its germ at the generic point has Laurent series the image of the Laurent series of $a \in K$ under coefficientwise application of $L \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$; and `hgal`, which says that for every automorphism $g$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ fixing $L$ pointwise and all $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$, if $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and `pullback.fst` equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, then $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x' =$ `arithmeticGalois (x1FunctionField (M*p)) g` applied to $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x$.
--
--   **Special-fibre group data.** An object $G$ of [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9), consisting of abelian groups $G.J_{0s}$, $G.J_I$, $G.J_E$, a subgroup `torus` of $G.J_{0s}$, and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj} : G.J_{0s} \to G.J_I \times G.J_E$ with kernel `torus`; bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` of $G.J_{0s}$, $G.J_I$, $G.J_E$ with the $k$-points of $D_k.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$; hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` stating that these bijections turn addition into tensor product of the pullbacks of the respective Poincaré bundles; and `hproj`, stating for each $x$ that `ptsI (G.proj x).1` is `pts x` post-composed with `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom i₁.1 i₁.2 hε₁ hreps hrep₁.some`, and `ptsE (G.proj x).2` is `pts x` post-composed with $\nu_2$.
--
--   **Generic points and Hecke action.** A bijection `gpts` between $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp) = \mathrm{Pic}^0(\bar{\mathbb{Q}},$ `x1FunctionFieldBar (M*p)` $)$ and the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $A$, with `hgadd` saying it is additive for the relative group law coming from `hrep.some` and `algEquivZeroGroupCut`; a map $\varphi$ from [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16) to endomorphisms of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, with `hφmul` saying each $\varphi(t)$ is additive for that relative group law on all test schemes, and `hφpts` saying that, for the module structure `heckeModuleOneBar (M*p)`, `gpts (t • x)` is `gpts x` followed by $\varphi(t)$.
--
--   **Abel–Jacobi data over $L$ and over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ (summarised here).** Representability `hDL` of the sub-Picard functor for $(X_L, \varepsilon_L)$ by $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L$; a morphism $a_{jL}$ from $X_L$ to $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L).\mathrm{toBase}$ over the base, with `hajLε` saying $\varepsilon_L$ followed by $a_{jL}$ is the zero section, and `hajL` saying that for every field $K'$, every $t : \operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every $K'$-point $x$ of $X_L$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` along $x$ followed by $a_{jL}$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of $t$ followed by $\varepsilon_L$; a morphism $k_L$ from $X_{\bar{\mathbb{Q}}}$ to $X_L$ compatible with both projections (`hkL₁`, `hkL₂`); a compatibility `hPL` of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` with the base change to $L$ of the pullback along `pullback.fst D.toBase (specMap A L)`; a morphism $\bar{a}_j$ from $M_\eta.C$ to $D.P$ defined by `hajbar` as $e_\eta$ followed by $k_L$, $a_{jL}$ and `pullback.fst`, lying over $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ followed by `specMap A (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` (`hajbar_over`); a $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\bar\varepsilon$ of $M_\eta.C$ inducing the point $\varepsilon$ of $X$ (`hεbar`) and sent by $\bar{a}_j$ to the zero section (`hεbar_aj`); and `hpts_aj`, which says that for all $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ inducing $\varepsilon$ there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M*p)` equal to the difference of the places of $x$ and of $s$ with `gpts (Pic0.mk Dv)` given by $x$ followed by $\bar{a}_j$.
--
--   **Igusa models and Frobenius.** An integral weight-one form $w$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ (a weight-one modular form with an integral power series $q$-expansion whose reduction over $k$ is nonzero); a curve model $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ over $k$ of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) with an isomorphism $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$ satisfying $e_1$ followed by $c_1$ equals $\mathrm{Mdl}_1.\mathrm{toBase}$; a nonemptiness hypothesis on the corresponding chart preimage in $\mathrm{Mdl}_1.C$; `hgauss₁`, which says that for $a$ in the finite chart algebra and power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction in $k$, if $a \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ then the element of the Igusa field obtained from $a$ through $e_1$, $i_1$ and `pullback.fst` has Laurent series the quotient of the reductions of $x$ and $y$ over $k$; an additive bijection $\theta_1$ from $G.J_I$ to $\mathrm{Pic}^0(k, \mathrm{Ig})$ with `hθpin₁`, which says that if for $g \in G.J_I$ and a $k$-point $x$ of $c_1$ the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₁.some` along `ptsI g` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of $\varepsilon_1$, then there is a degree-zero divisor equal to the difference of the places of $x$ and $\varepsilon_1$ computed through $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ whose class is $\theta_1 g$; an element `frobIg` of `SemilinearAut k Ig` (a pair of ring automorphisms of the Igusa field and of $k$ compatible with the structure map) acting on Laurent coefficients by $p$-th powers (`hfrobIg`); and a second curve model $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$ over $k$ of the same Igusa field with an isomorphism $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ satisfying $e_2$ followed by $c_2$ equals $\mathrm{Mdl}_2.\mathrm{toBase}$.
--
--   **Place data.** A valuation subring $\mathrm{Pl}$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit in it, a ring homomorphism $\rho : A \to \mathrm{Pl}$ whose composite with the inclusion is the structure map $A \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, a subring $O \le \mathrm{Pl}$ with a homomorphism $\rho_O : A \to O$ compatible in the same way, and a surjective ring homomorphism $\pi_k : \mathrm{Pl} \to k$ with $A \to k$ equal to $\pi_k \circ \rho$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist maps
--   $$\mathrm{red}_1, \mathrm{red}_2 : \mathrm{Place}\,\bar{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}\,(M*p)) \longrightarrow \mathrm{Place}\,k\,(\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,k\,M\,w)$$
--   such that both of the following hold.
--
--   First, for every place $P$, every $O$-point $\xi$ of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\rho_O$ (that is, $\xi$ with $\xi$ followed by $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}\rho_O$) and every $k$-point $c$ of $c_1$: if $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $O \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $\xi$ equals the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}(P)$ followed by $e_\eta$ and `pullback.fst`, and if $c$ followed by $i_1$ and `pullback.fst` equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\pi_k \circ (O \hookrightarrow \mathrm{Pl})$ followed by $\xi$, then $\mathrm{red}_1 P = \mathrm{Mdl}_1.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ of the $k$-point $c$ followed by $e_1^{-1}$.
--
--   Second, the same statement with $i_1$, $c_1$, $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$, $e_1$, $\mathrm{red}_1$ replaced by $i_2$, $c_2$, $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$, $e_2$, $\mathrm{red}_2$: for every place $P$, every $O$-point $\xi$ of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\rho_O$ and every $k$-point $c$ of $c_2$, if $\operatorname{Spec}(O \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb{Q}})$ followed by $\xi$ is the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-point attached to $P$ through $M_\eta$ and $e_\eta$, and $c$ followed by $i_2$ and `pullback.fst` is the reduction of $\xi$ along $\pi_k$, then $\mathrm{red}_2 P = \mathrm{Mdl}_2.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ of $c$ followed by $e_2^{-1}$.
--
--   This provides the place-level reduction dictionary between places of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}(X_1(Mp))$ and places of the Igusa function field over $k$, attached to the two components of the special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$; the two clauses of the conclusion are exactly the form in which the reduction maps are consumed further on. It is used in the computations of the Frobenius and Hecke/diamond action on the second component of the special fibre of the Néron model of $J_1(Mp)$.
